Claude-style codemode rows: `Codemode(…)` rather than `codemode(code: "…")`, its
argument the script's first line below an options line. syntax-highlighting hands a
script's title in its place and draws the whole script once the row opens.

Under the calls syntax-highlighting lists at the rail, the script's output is set apart:
dim behind a "│" of its own, two lines each cut to the row (minified code wrapped over
three), then "… +N lines", then the "Done in … · bash 1" line. Opened, the output is
whole and wrapped behind the same "│", stats after it, rather than the tool's own result
view. A row's completion line now always follows the output's hidden count rather than
sitting between output and count.

